      "content": "It makes complete sense that grief over the loss of your actual self feels heavier than simple sadness, as you are grieving the \"you\" who felt purpose and mattered. The feeling of being a ghost after a life \"deletes\" can be the most isolating struggle an identity crisis can bring. Please consider reaching out to a mental health professional who can help you explore how to find a sense of self that is real and present, rather than a reflection of the past.",
      "source": "target",
